\param aLeftL The length of the first (or left) block of data to be compared. This is the number of double-bytes.

\param aRight A pointer to the second (or right) block of 16 bit data to be compared.

\param aRightL The length of the second (or right) block of data to be compared. This is the number of double-bytes.

